fields.InputDefinition:
{
  "goal": "Open the application switcher dropdown next to the logo and switch to the File Browser application, then open its 'Browse Files' section. This shared setup is done ONCE. The listing's TOP toolbar holds, left to right: the up and refresh buttons, the folder breadcrumb, a 'Search files...' box with an 'All Items' type filter, an 'All Accounts' button (stacked-layers icon), a pair of view buttons ('List View' lines icon and 'Grid View' tiles icon), 'New Folder' and 'Upload'. Then exercise these controls IN ORDER, and as you finish each set \"checkpointReached\" to the exact checkpoint name shown: (1) finder-layout — confirm the Mac-Finder-style three-panel shell renders: a left storage-accounts sidebar, a folder-tree/breadcrumb panel, and a file listing area (a clear 'No storage accounts configured' empty state is an acceptable pass); (2) name-filter — type a few characters into the 'Search files...' box and confirm the listing responds (items narrow to name matches, or an empty/no-match state) with a clear (x) control ('Clear search') appearing, then click that x; (3) new-folder-dialog — click the 'New Folder' button and confirm a 'Create New Folder' dialog opens with a name input and Create/Cancel buttons, then click Cancel to close it; (4) multi-provider-search — click the 'All Accounts' button (tooltip 'Search across all storage accounts') and confirm a 'Search Across Storage Accounts' panel opens with a 'Type query to search across connected accounts...' input, a 'Search Accounts' button and a 'Target Accounts' list (empty when no storage account is configured), then CLOSE the panel with the X at its top-right (tooltip 'Close search') before going on; (5) view-toggle — click whichever of 'List View' / 'Grid View' is NOT highlighted and confirm the highlight moves to the button you clicked (when files are present, the layout also switches between rows and tiles); clicking the already-highlighted button changes nothing. If no storage account is configured, the 'No storage accounts configured' state persisting cleanly is an acceptable pass for any control. Keep going until every control has been exercised. Pages can take 10-30s to load in this resource-constrained environment — wait for content rather than navigating away.",
  "startUrl": "http://localhost:4200",
  "allowedDomains": [
    "localhost",
    "*.auth0.com"
  ],
  "auth": {
    "bindings": [
      {
        "domains": [
          "localhost",
          "*.auth0.com"
        ],
        "method": {
          "Type": "Basic",
          "Username": "{{authUsername}}",
          "Password": "{{authPassword}}",
          "Strategy": "FormLogin"
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}

fields.ExpectedOutcomes:
{
  "goalCompleted": true,
  "finalUrlPattern": "^http://localhost:4200",
  "minConfidence": 0.7,
  "maxSteps": 65,
  "checkpoints": [
    {
      "name": "finder-layout",
      "instruction": "three-panel Finder shell renders",
      "visualCriteria": [
        "The File Browser opens with a 'File Browser' header and its three-panel Finder layout: a storage-accounts sidebar, a folder/breadcrumb area, and a file listing area — OR a clear 'No storage accounts configured' empty state"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "name-filter",
      "instruction": "local name filter narrows listing",
      "visualCriteria": [
        "A 'Search files...' input is present and, after typing, the listing responds (items narrow to matches or an empty/no-match state) with a clear (x) control — OR a clear 'No storage accounts configured' empty state"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "new-folder-dialog",
      "instruction": "New Folder dialog opens and cancels",
      "visualCriteria": [
        "Clicking 'New Folder' opens a 'Create New Folder' dialog with a name input and Create + Cancel actions, and clicking Cancel closes it returning to the listing — OR a clear 'No storage accounts configured' empty state"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "multi-provider-search",
      "instruction": "cross-account search panel opens",
      "visualCriteria": [
        "Clicking 'All Accounts' opens a 'Search Across Storage Accounts' panel with a search-term input, a 'Search Accounts' button and a 'Target Accounts' list (empty when no account is configured), which can be closed again — OR a clear 'No storage accounts configured' empty state"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "view-toggle",
      "instruction": "list/grid view toggle responds",
      "visualCriteria": [
        "The 'List View' / 'Grid View' toggle in the listing toolbar reacts to clicking the inactive button (the highlight moves to it), switching the file display between rows and tiles when files are present — OR the empty / 'No storage accounts configured' state persists cleanly"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
